    {
      "slug": "can-smart-locks-keep-privacy",
      "title": "Every smart lock promises privacy. Can any of them keep it?",
      "tags": [
        "tech",
        "policy",
        "report"
      ],
      "daysAgo": 3,
      "markdown": "We tested a stack of connected locks and read every privacy policy. Most collect more than they need, and few explain why.\n\n## What we looked for\n\n- Does it work without an account?\n- Where are the logs stored, and for how long?\n- Can you delete your history?\n\nOnly two passed all three. A report like this is the template's lead story; this one is placeholder copy.",
      "excerpt": "We tested the locks and read the policies. Two passed.",
      "featured": true,
      "coverUrl": "/api/assets/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "coverAlt": "Abstract placeholder artwork",
      "authors": [
        "sam-rivera"
      ],
      "commentsEnabled": true
    },
    {
